        "title": "Convergent Evolution: Conway Morris vs Gould",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Conway Morris vs Gould debate is one of evolutionary biology's deepest arguments: is evolution deterministic (similar selective pressures reliably produce similar outcomes) or contingent (the history of life depends on unpredictable accidents)? Their direct disagreement about the Cambrian Burgess Shale fauna crystallized into a broader argument about whether evolution would replay the same way if the tape were run again. Both positions are partially correct, and the resolution involves understanding when convergence is expected vs when it is absent."
    }
